    "title": "Actor Patrick Muldoon suffers heart attack, dies at 57",
    "text": "Updated April 20, 2026, 11:03 a.m. ETActor Patrick Muldoon died suddenly on Sunday, April 19 at age 57, his manager announced.An award-winning actor, producer and musician, Muldoon rose to fame in the 1990s for roles in hit soap operas like \"Days of Our Lives,\" and \"Melrose Place,\" later expanding to producing films, and in 2019, he released an EP, according to IMDb.Muldoon's manager confirmed his death to Variety and Deadline reported the cause of death as a heart attack.Muldoon is survived by his partner Miriam Rothbert, his parents, sister and brother-in-law and a niece and nephew, per Variety.Here's what to know about Patrick Muldoon.Did Patrick Muldoon die?Yes, Patrick Muldoon died April 19 at age 57, Variety reported, citing Muldoon's manager.Who was Patrick Muldoon?Born William Patrick Muldoon III in San Pedro, California and known as Patrick Muldoon, he was an award-winning actor, producer and musician, per IMDb.He was known for starring in the TV series \"Saved By the Bell,\" daytime soap opera \"Days of Our Lives,\" primetime soap \"Melrose Place,\" and the sci-fi film \"Starship Troopers,\" later returning to \"Days of Our Lives.\"He also produced films and in 2019 released an EP \"Muldoon and Ives.\"How did Patrick Muldoon die?Muldoon died unexpectedly of a heart attack, Deadline reported.Contact Jenna Prestininzi: jprestininzi@freepress.com.",
